{{also|face-value}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
The term exists because a contrast between [[nominal value]] and [[market value]] is sometimes materially relevant for currencies.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-face value.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[amount]] or value listed on a [[bill]], [[note]], [[stamp]], etc.; the stated value or amount.
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} No more or less than what is stated; a [[literal]] or [[direct]] meaning or interpretation.
#: {{ux|en|Please take this comment at '''face value''' and don't try to read anything into it.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 June 3|author=Sam Mullins OBE discusses with Stefanie Foster|title=LTM: a new chapter begins at 40|journal=Rail|page=52|text=Few museums have such a coherent collection that covers so many different areas of interest as the London Transport Museum. At '''face value''', it is a collection of urban transport in London. In reality, it is so much more.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|par value}}

